 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "System",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Wires are crimped into SPH contacts, the contacts snap into a PHR housing, and the housing plugs into a shrouded header on the board. Mounted height is 8.0 mm with a top-entry through-hole header and its housing; the system is 4.5 mm wide. Headers have a board retention feature, and an SMT version is made."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Contacts",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "SPH-002T-P0.5S takes 0.05 to 0.22 mm² (AWG 30 to 24) with insulation 0.9 to 1.5 mm across; SPH-002T-P0.5L takes 0.08 to 0.22 mm² (AWG 28 to 24), 0.8 to 1.5 mm; SPH-004T-P0.5S takes 0.032 to 0.08 mm² (AWG 32 to 28), 0.5 to 0.9 mm. All crimp on the AP-K2N machine with the matching applicator."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Through-hole board layout",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Holes are 0.7 mm (+0.1/0) on a 2 mm pitch, centres held to ±0.05 mm, non-cumulative. Hole size varies with board material and piercing method; boards of hard material take larger holes. The hole figures are guidance."
  },
  {
   "topic": "SMT board layout",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each SM4 header has a row of signal pads at least 1 mm wide on a 2 mm pitch and one larger pad for the solder tab at each end. Pad centres are held to ±0.05 mm, non-cumulative; the pad figures are guidance."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Labelling",
   "page": 2,
